<title>UK: Novorossiisk, Ventspils oil ports closed - source.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk, Ventspils oil ports closed - source.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea and Latvia's Ventspils oil port on the Baltic remained closed on Monday due to bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk, which was closed for much of last week, reopened briefly on Sunday before closing again later that day.</p>
<p>Ventpils closed at 0200 local time on Sunday, the source said. It was also closed for about 24 hours from Tuesday to Wednesday last week due to high winds.</p>
<p>Bad weather has kept Novorossiisk closed for much of February, leading to loading delays of about five days.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea oil ports at Odessa and Tuapse were operating normally.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
